#1 positive.ts:1:1-4.4 - comments-in-file-header: use of docstring/explanatory comments in file header.
#2 positive.ts:5:30-34 - ts-prefer-node-protocol: prefer the `node:` protocol when importing a Node.js builtin module, as it makes clear that the module is a builtin (`"fs"` -> `"node:fs"`).
#3 positive.ts:7:1-17 - decorative-comment: use of banner or separator comments made of repeated characters.
#4 positive.ts:9:1-47 - redundant-docstring: documentation only restates the name of the declaration.
#5 positive.ts:11:3-42 - step-comment: use of numbered or sequenced comments that narrate the steps of the code.
#6 positive.ts:13:3-43 - narrating-comment: comment narrates what the code does instead of explaining why.
